  "slug": "learning-biology-small-c2ee",
  "summary": "New work scores generated molecules by PBPK exposure and multistage filtration, exposing attrition that standard generation metrics miss.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is constraint-driven molecular generation and screening, with evaluation increasingly moved downstream of model architecture. PharmaDiff conditions 3D diffusion on pharmacophores, PFM uses a perturbed conditional probability path for pocket-conditioned flow matching, and SF-GA redesigns predicted P-gp substrates into synthetically accessible predicted nonsubstrates. A rule-defined PEG library (~123M generated, ~50M retained) extends the screening space. The newer element is evaluation: HEDGEHOG's six-stage filtration of 22 generators on KRAS G12D shows attrition that standard metrics miss, and PBPK-based re-scoring of PARP1 candidates shows exposure and safety limits reshuffling rankings. Carvedilol as a partial THRβ agonist, supported by TR-FRET and cell lipid assays, is the only item with experimental confirmation.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-12"
}
